# Binary allowlist for the no-binary-bytes CI gate.
#
# Every tracked file in this repository is text. The gate rejects any tracked
# file containing a NUL byte (0x00) — the byte that makes git and most text
# tooling treat a file as binary, at which point grep -I skips it silently and
# exits 0. This file is the ONLY escape hatch.
#
# Each non-comment line is a git pathspec (relative to the repo root) that is
# excluded from the scan. Examples (do not enable without review):
#   docs/img/architecture.png
#   */src/test/resources/fixtures/*.bin
#
# It ships EMPTY on purpose, and that is currently a statement of fact rather
# than an aspiration: all tracked files are text. A genuinely binary asset —
# an image, a keystore, a compiled fixture — is the only thing that belongs
# here. A source file with a stray control character does not: write the
# character as a language-level escape instead.

